                <div class="tab-content top">
                    <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="tabpanel-57a41338d0cc408b99d1ca06cdfa3eed-0" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-57a41338d0cc408b99d1ca06cdfa3eed-0" tabindex="0">
                        <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <h2>Division of Land Protection - Remediation Branch</h2>

    
    

</div>


    
    
    <div class="containers tn-accordion parbase">
    <div class="accordion" id="accordion-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd">
        

        
            

            
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    

                    
                        <div class="accordion-heading">
                            <span class="accordion-title">
                                <button class="accordion-button icon-angle-right collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-0" aria-controls="collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-0" aria-expanded="false">
                                    Atomic City Auto (Oak Ridge, Anderson County)
                                </button>
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <div id="collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-0" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordion-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd">
                            <div class="accordion-body panel-body" tabindex="0">
                                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-textandimage textimage parbase">



<div class="textimage-left" style="float: left;">
<div  id="cq-image-jsp-/content/tn/environment/program-areas/rem-remediation/tnclean/jcr:content/content/tn_tabs_copy/parsys_east_tn_sites/tn_accordion/parsys_atomic_city_autooakridgeandersoncounty/tn_textandimage/image"><a href="/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/atomic-city-images/rem_tnclean-atomic-city-b25-box_01-26-2004.PNG"><img src="/environment/program-areas/rem-remediation/tnclean/_jcr_content/content/tn_tabs_copy/parsys_east_tn_sites/tn_accordion/parsys_atomic_city_autooakridgeandersoncounty/tn_textandimage/image.img.png/1747686104233.png" alt="A B-25 box containing radioactive material removed from the Atomic City site sits in a dirt plane along with rusty equipment, dead trees, piles of dirt and cylinders, and construction supplies. " title="A B-25 box containing radioactive material on the Atomic City Auto Parts site. " class="cq-dd-image"></a></div>

    
<script type="text/javascript">
    (function() {
        var imageDiv = document.getElementById("cq\u002Dimage\u002Djsp\u002D\/content\/tn\/environment\/program\u002Dareas\/rem\u002Dremediation\/tnclean\/jcr:content\/content\/tn_tabs_copy\/parsys_east_tn_sites\/tn_accordion\/parsys_atomic_city_autooakridgeandersoncounty\/tn_textandimage\/image");
        var imageEvars = '{ imageLink: "/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/atomic-city-images/rem_tnclean-atomic-city-b25-box_01-26-2004.PNG", imageAsset: "/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/atomic-city-images/rem_tnclean-atomic-city-b25-box_01-26-2004.PNG", imageTitle: "A B\u002D25 box containing radioactive material on the Atomic City Auto Parts site. " }';
        var tagNodes = imageDiv.getElementsByTagName('A');
        for (var i = 0; i < tagNodes.length; i++) {
            var link = tagNodes.item(i); 
            link.setAttribute('onclick', 'CQ_Analytics.record({event: "imageClick", values: ' + imageEvars + ', collect: false, options: { obj: this }, componentPath: "tncore\/components\/content\/tn\u002Dimage"})');
        }
        
    })();
</script>


</div>
<div class="textimage-text">
    
        <p>The Atomic City Auto Parts site was a former automobile junkyard and scrap metal recycling facility located in Oak Ridge. DoR used a state remediation contractor to complete an interim removal action in 2003-2004 as part of a negotiated agreement with US Department of Energy (DOE), who was the responsible party. Contaminated soil and debris was excavated and removed for offsite. TDEC conducted a cleanup of this site that was completed in 2005. Based upon a review of TDEC&#39;s confirmatory sampling conducted after cleanup was completed, the DOE believes that TDEC &#39;s cleanup objectives for the site have been met and TDEC concurred in a letter to DOE in October 2021. The only remaining actions for this site are development of a Risk Assessment (assigned to DOE), development of a Record of Decision, recording of a Notice of Land Use Restriction (NLUR) and the delisting process.  No further remediation is required.</p>

    
    

</div>


<div class="clear"></div></div>


</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    
                </div>
            
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    

                    
                        <div class="accordion-heading">
                            <span class="accordion-title">
                                <button class="accordion-button icon-angle-right collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-1" aria-controls="collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-1" aria-expanded="false">
                                    Former Mark IV Electro-Voice (Newport, Cocke County)
                                </button>
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <div id="collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordion-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd">
                            <div class="accordion-body panel-body" tabindex="0">
                                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-textandimage textimage parbase">



<div class="textimage-top" style="float: initial;">
<div  id="cq-image-jsp-/content/tn/environment/program-areas/rem-remediation/tnclean/jcr:content/content/tn_tabs_copy/parsys_east_tn_sites/tn_accordion/parsys_former_mark_iv_electro-voicenewportcockecounty/tn_textandimage/image"><a href="/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/mark-iv-images/rem_tnclean-mark-iv-warehouse-floor_09-11-2023.PNG"><img src="/environment/program-areas/rem-remediation/tnclean/_jcr_content/content/tn_tabs_copy/parsys_east_tn_sites/tn_accordion/parsys_former_mark_iv_electro-voicenewportcockecounty/tn_textandimage/image.img.png/1703103316313.png" alt="Stored goods in the Mark IV warehouse" title="Stored goods in the Mark IV warehouse" class="cq-dd-image"></a></div>

    
<script type="text/javascript">
    (function() {
        var imageDiv = document.getElementById("cq\u002Dimage\u002Djsp\u002D\/content\/tn\/environment\/program\u002Dareas\/rem\u002Dremediation\/tnclean\/jcr:content\/content\/tn_tabs_copy\/parsys_east_tn_sites\/tn_accordion\/parsys_former_mark_iv_electro\u002Dvoicenewportcockecounty\/tn_textandimage\/image");
        var imageEvars = '{ imageLink: "/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/mark-iv-images/rem_tnclean-mark-iv-warehouse-floor_09-11-2023.PNG", imageAsset: "/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/mark-iv-images/rem_tnclean-mark-iv-warehouse-floor_09-11-2023.PNG", imageTitle: "Stored goods in the Mark IV warehouse" }';
        var tagNodes = imageDiv.getElementsByTagName('A');
        for (var i = 0; i < tagNodes.length; i++) {
            var link = tagNodes.item(i); 
            link.setAttribute('onclick', 'CQ_Analytics.record({event: "imageClick", values: ' + imageEvars + ', collect: false, options: { obj: this }, componentPath: "tncore\/components\/content\/tn\u002Dimage"})');
        }
        
    })();
</script>


</div>
<div class="textimage-text">
    
        <p>This property was an audio speaker assembly plant for the company Electro-Voice, previously owned by Mark IV Industries. The assembly plant was in operation from the mid 1960s until 2001. This former industrial site has been monitored since 2001 for chlorinated solvent chemicals that leaked from an underground storage tank. Groundwater, soil, and air on this property have been sampled for these cleaning chemicals to ensure that the concentrations are low enough to be safe for workers on the site now and in the future.  Groundwater contamination is currently present in three monitoring wells at the property.</p>

    
    

</div>


<div class="clear"></div></div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-linkbuttons"><div>
	
        <div>
            
            
                <a href="https://arcg.is/1S4zD50" target="_blank" class="button red">Explore the Mark IV StoryMap</a>
            
        </div>
	
</div></div>


</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    
                </div>
            
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    

                    
                        <div class="accordion-heading">
                            <span class="accordion-title">
                                <button class="accordion-button icon-angle-right collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-2" aria-controls="collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-2" aria-expanded="false">
                                    Wall Tube &amp; Metal (Newport, Cocke County) 
                                </button>
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <div id="collapse-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd-2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordion-4f557cc2346444b393eae9c9f5ab5dcd">
                            <div class="accordion-body panel-body" tabindex="0">
                                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-textandimage textimage parbase">



<div class="textimage-left" style="float: left;">
<div  id="cq-image-jsp-/content/tn/environment/program-areas/rem-remediation/tnclean/jcr:content/content/tn_tabs_copy/parsys_east_tn_sites/tn_accordion/parsys_wall_tube_metal_newportcockecounty/tn_textandimage/image"><a href="/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/wall-tube-metals-images/rem_tnclean-wall-tube-excavation_09-26-2023.PNG"><img src="/environment/program-areas/rem-remediation/tnclean/_jcr_content/content/tn_tabs_copy/parsys_east_tn_sites/tn_accordion/parsys_wall_tube_metal_newportcockecounty/tn_textandimage/image.img.png/1703102779872.png" alt="An excavator bulldozer rests the digging arm on a crushed rusty metal drum containing a strange greenish oxide in a large dirt pit." title="Excavator digs out a crushed drum containing unknown materials on the Wall Tube &amp; Metals site." class="cq-dd-image"></a></div>

    
<script type="text/javascript">
    (function() {
        var imageDiv = document.getElementById("cq\u002Dimage\u002Djsp\u002D\/content\/tn\/environment\/program\u002Dareas\/rem\u002Dremediation\/tnclean\/jcr:content\/content\/tn_tabs_copy\/parsys_east_tn_sites\/tn_accordion\/parsys_wall_tube_metal_newportcockecounty\/tn_textandimage\/image");
        var imageEvars = '{ imageLink: "/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/wall-tube-metals-images/rem_tnclean-wall-tube-excavation_09-26-2023.PNG", imageAsset: "/content/dam/tn/environment/remediation/images/tn-clean/wall-tube-metals-images/rem_tnclean-wall-tube-excavation_09-26-2023.PNG", imageTitle: "Excavator digs out a crushed drum containing unknown materials on the Wall Tube \x26 Metals site." }';
        var tagNodes = imageDiv.getElementsByTagName('A');
        for (var i = 0; i < tagNodes.length; i++) {
            var link = tagNodes.item(i); 
            link.setAttribute('onclick', 'CQ_Analytics.record({event: "imageClick", values: ' + imageEvars + ', collect: false, options: { obj: this }, componentPath: "tncore\/components\/content\/tn\u002Dimage"})');
        }
        
    })();
</script>


</div>
<div class="textimage-text">
    
        <p>Wall Tube &amp; Metal Products operated at the site from 1956 to 1983, manufacturing steel tubing and conducting metal plating and fabrication activities for industrial and commercial applications. Since 1983, multiple manufacturers have operated at the site. The property encompasses approximately 16 acres and is currently used for furniture manufacturing.</p>
<p>Previous and ongoing investigations have identified chlorinated solvents as a primary chemical of concern. Chlorinated solvents have been detected in groundwater at the site, with detections also identified historically in off-site surface water downgradient from the site.</p>
<p>In 1985, waste materials associated with prior operations were removed. A TDEC report issued in 1986 identified metal plating sludge, paint sludge, and chlorinated solvents as contaminants of concern at the site. During the late 1980s and early 1990s, TDEC and the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency evaluated the nature and extent of contamination and developed remedial plans.</p>
<p>In 1997, the Tennessee Department of Remediation removed 350 cubic yards of contaminated soil from the facility. A site investigation conducted in 2005 found that chlorinated solvent contamination remained present in groundwater and indicated the potential for off-site migration.</p>
<p>Recent groundwater investigations conducted since 2023 indicate that chlorinated solvent contamination in groundwater has the potential to be migrating off-site. Ongoing groundwater, soil gas, and indoor air investigations are being conducted to further define the extent of contamination and refine understanding of site conditions.</p>

    
    

</div>


<div class="clear"></div></div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-linkbuttons"><div>
	
        <div>
            
            
                <a href="https://arcg.is/1L9C511" target="_blank" class="button red">Explore the Wall Tube &amp; Metal StoryMap</a>
            
        </div>
	
</div></div>


</div>
